&gt;&gt;Tim Ferris: Sure, David, thanks for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:31.600 --> 00:57:38.080
question. Well, first, maybe I'll emphasise&nbsp;
some similarities. And the similarities are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:39.200 --> 00:57:44.240
the genuine effort to make the process work,&nbsp;
the staffing and financing, all the things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:44.240 --> 00:57:52.240
that I heard Emily so wonderfully review are&nbsp;
all, the challenges are largely the same.&nbsp;

00:57:53.040 --> 00:57:56.640
Also, filling the information&nbsp;
gap for the population&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:57:57.760 --> 00:58:06.160
to address vaccine hesitancy is top of mind. And&nbsp;
the proactive concerns about the potential for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:06.720 --> 00:58:11.840
inequity in health outcomes resulting from&nbsp;
unequal uptake are very much top of mind.&nbsp;

00:58:12.640 --> 00:58:21.120
I will then make a contrast, which is, you&nbsp;
know, in the US, the supply chain process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:21.120 --> 00:58:28.240
from manufacturer to federal government, to state&nbsp;
government, and then to the variable set of end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:29.760 --> 00:58:36.160
jabbers is, it's very different the way&nbsp;
it's being managed in the US. And I will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:36.160 --> 00:58:42.320
say that the coordination of the&nbsp;
many players in the supply chain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:43.040 --> 00:58:50.080
and the lack of visibility of each player to the&nbsp;
other in the supply chain is a really big problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:58:50.080 --> 00:58:56.640
in the US that is creating enormous amounts&nbsp;
of inefficiency and ineffectiveness.&nbsp;

00:58:57.600 --> 00:59:04.640
And so, I contrast with that with the end-to-end&nbsp;
visibility that I see, that I hear described by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:04.640 --> 00:59:12.400
Emily, and I'm, I'm frankly, jealous. It is&nbsp;
clearly more, more effective, and efficient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:12.400 --> 00:59:16.720
to have that end-to-end visibility,&nbsp;
which does not exist in United States.&nbsp;

00:59:16.720 --> 00:59:23.120
And then I'll just close by saying that, you&nbsp;
know, of course, we also share going back to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:59:23.120 --> 00:59:29.920
