&gt;&gt;Simon Stevens:&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:01:57.760 --> 01:02:01.280
No, although, well, just a reflection on&nbsp;
the vaccines conversation we just had.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:01.280 --> 01:02:06.720
Look, we're not there yet. We've, we're off to a&nbsp;
strong start, we've got good momentum, but there&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:06.720 --> 01:02:15.040
is a huge journey ahead of us still. We are as&nbsp;
has been now well vetted in public discourse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:15.840 --> 01:02:21.120
you know, supply constrained, and so there is,&nbsp;
you know, unevenness, day by day through the week&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:21.120 --> 01:02:27.760
and week by week. And, you know, we're on&nbsp;
track for where we want to be by the 15th of&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:27.760 --> 01:02:31.760
February. But as I previously said,&nbsp;
it's two sprints, and then a marathon.&nbsp;

01:02:31.760 --> 01:02:36.640
So, you know, this is the first sprint. The&nbsp;
second sprint will be the next group of at-risk&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:36.640 --> 01:02:41.760
individuals identified by JCVI and government,&nbsp;
and then the marathon will be extending to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:41.760 --> 01:02:45.440
whole population. And we're going to&nbsp;
continue to adjust the model as we go.&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:46.240 --> 01:02:54.400
As we have more supply, then more High Street&nbsp;
pharmacists and other easily convenient access&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:02:54.400 --> 01:03:00.240
points will be available. And we'll have more&nbsp;
of the larger scale vaccination offers as well.&nbsp;

01:03:00.240 --> 01:03:05.040
But for right now, about three-quarters of&nbsp;
the vaccines that have been delivered have&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:03:05.040 --> 01:03:11.200
been delivered through primary care through GP-led&nbsp;
